body:
fdp's output for graphs with clusters can change from one C run to the next on the same machine. Derived graphs orient their edges and order their ports by node address, and macOS's allocator sometimes gives the freed nodes of one derived graph back to the next one and sometimes gives fresh addresses. On the reproducer C produced two different drawings in 20 runs (16 vs 4). The port has a deterministic allocator model and always produces the more frequent one.

**Reproducer**

```dot
graph "G" {
layout=fdp;
subgraph "cluster_2" {
"n6";
"n32" [fixedsize="false"];
}
subgraph "cluster_6" {
"n4";
"n30" [];
}
"n4" -- "n41";
"n4" -- "n13";
"n4" -- "n6":"_" [label="e=mc²", arrowtail="crow"];
}
```

```sh
GVBINDIR=<pango-free plugins> dot -Kfdp -Tsvg repro.gv   # C Graphviz 16.1.0
graphviz-pure -Kfdp -Tsvg repro.gv                              # port
```

**C output vs port**

```diff

```

**Root cause**

C compares `Agnode_t *` pointers in `lib/fdpgen/layout.c:466` (`if (hd > tl)` when creating derived edges), `:501` (`if (dn > m)` for port edges) and `:634` (`if (n < other)` in `genPorts`, which sets the order and angles of a multi-edge's ports). An instrumented C build (`GVDBG3=1`) logs the derived nodes' addresses, and its output tracks their order exactly. On the reproducer, in 24 runs, the derived graph of `cluster_6` got its nodes in the order `n4, n30, port...` 8 times (output A) and `port, n30, n4, ...` 16 times (output B), always matching the output. The port models the allocator in `crates/graphviz-pure-layout/src/fdpgen/layout.rs:127-160` (`NodeHeap`: LIFO reuse of freed slots, then fresh increasing addresses) and orients by that model at `layout.rs:607,637,740`.

**Why the port cannot match**

C's result depends on heap addresses, which vary between runs, so no deterministic port can match every run. The port follows the allocation pattern C shows most often. On the reproducer and on seed 12476 that is C's most frequent output. Seeds 31247 and 35776 have 9 and 8 different C outputs in 20 runs, and the port matches one of them. For seed 12476 the two C variants differ only in one record text coordinate (22.62 vs 22.63); the address-dependent path was not traced for that seed. A fix would have to come from upstream: order derived nodes by `ND_id`/creation order instead of by pointer.

**Cases**

3 fuzz case(s), seeds 12476, 31247, 35776. Other fdp cases also vary run to run in C, but they also needed a port fix and are listed under that fix's issue. Regenerate one with `python3 -I scripts/fuzz-gen.py --seed N` (byte for byte for every seed listed here).

**Files**

`tests/fuzz-open/025-fdp-cluster-address-dependent-layout`

Visual diff: {{SITE}}/whats-left/fdp-cluster-address-dependent-layout/

With `sametail` (or `samehead`) on a record node, `sameport` rounds the merged port to whole points. That can put the port just outside the record's outermost field. C's `record_path` then finds no field and still returns the side mask without filling in any box, so `beginpath`/`endpath` keep whatever `endp->boxes`/`boxn` happened to be on the stack. C's edges then start up to 100pt away from the node (seed 1278). In seed 1153 (`rankdir=RL`) C's `Pshortestpath` fails, the edge `name 86 -> name 87` is lost, and C exits 1. The port uses the node box instead and draws a normal edge from the node boundary.

**Reproducer**

```dot
digraph "fuzz 1278" {
"n3" [shape="record", label="{{{\N}|<p0> long field text|<p1> long field text}}"];
subgraph "cluster_0" {
"n2" [];
"n6" [];
"n4" [];
}
"n0" -> "n3" [penwidth="2.25", weight="1"];
"n2" -> "n4" [label="中文标签\rfoo_bar\rthen", dir="none"];
"n3" -> "n2":"w" [weight="1", sametail="st1"];
"n3" -> "n6" [headport="e", weight="2", sametail="st1"];
{"n1" "n6" "n0"} -> "n0":"nw";
"n4" -> "n6" [headclip="false", lhead="cluster_0"];
}
```

```sh
GVBINDIR=<pango-free plugins> dot -Kdot -Tsvg repro.gv   # C Graphviz 16.1.0
graphviz-pure -Kdot -Tsvg repro.gv                               # port
```

**C output vs port**

```diff
--- c.svg
+++ rust.svg
-<path fill="none" stroke="black" d="M126,-52C126,-52 134.47,-148.23 88,-194.4 65.44,-216.81 38.89,-187.79 18.75,-212.4 17.16,-214.34 15.69,-216.82 14.65,-219.32"/>
+<path fill="none" stroke="black" d="M126,-119.5C126,-119.5 117.08,-170.99 88,-194.4 63.23,-214.34 38.89,-187.79 18.75,-212.4 17.16,-214.34 15.69,-216.82 14.65,-219.32"/>
-<path fill="none" stroke="black" d="M126,-212.4C126,-212.4 157.86,-51 90.44,-35.23"/>
-<polygon fill="black" stroke="black" points="91.08,-31.78 80.76,-34.17 90.31,-38.74 91.08,-31.78"/>
+<path fill="none" stroke="black" d="M126,-117.5C126,-117.5 122.54,-48.92 90.23,-36.06"/>
+<polygon fill="black" stroke="black" points="91.21,-32.69 80.74,-34.28 89.92,-39.57 91.21,-32.69"/>
```

**Root cause**

`sameport` sets `prt.p = {round(x1), round(y1)}` (`lib/dotgen/sameport.c:149`). For the record in the reproducer the boundary point is x = -109.54 relative to the centre, so the rounded port x = -110 is outside field 0 (`LL.x = -109.54`). `record_path` (`lib/common/shapes.c:3793-3829`) loops over the fields, matches none (`BETWEEN(ls, p.x, rs)` fails) and still `return side`. `beginpath` (`lib/common/splines.c:542-543`, and `endpath` at `:740-741`) treats the non-zero return as success and skips the `endp->boxes[0] = endp->nb; endp->boxn = 1` fallback. But `tend`/`hend` in `make_regular_edge` are uninitialised locals (`pathend_t tend, hend;`, `lib/dotgen/dotsplines.c:1713`), so the box count and boxes are undefined behaviour. C's output is stable from run to run on one build but depends on stack contents.

The port's `pboxfn` (`crates/graphviz-pure-layout/src/dotgen/splinegraph.rs:166-195`) deliberately returns `None` in this case, which falls back to the node box (see the comment there). Confirmed by changing the record to `shape=box`: both programs then agree on both cases.

Why the port should not match: what C does depends on uninitialised stack memory, and reproducing it would mean modelling a particular C build's stack. Suggest closing as wontfix (upstream bug: `record_path` should return 0 when no field contains the port, or `tend`/`hend` should be zero-initialised).

**Cases**

2 fuzz case(s): seeds 1278, 1153. Seed 1153 (`rankdir=RL`, record `name 86` with `tailport=p0` and `sametail`) is the exit-status case: C prints `triangulation failed`, `source point not in any triangle`, `in routesplines, Pshortestpath failed` and `lost name 86 name 87 edge`, then exits 1. The port exits 0 and draws the edge.
Regenerate a case with `python3 -I scripts/fuzz-gen.py --seed N` (checked byte for byte for seed 1278).

